**Verdict: MAJOR REVISION.** I found no fatal error in the average-case theorem or Theorem 1.2. The remaining problems concern the specification and proof of the worst-case extraction cost, the precise interpretation of the lower bound, the moment-barrier claim, and incomplete appendix proofs.

The source changed during this review. All line references below refer to this [frozen source snapshot](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/paper_r17_review/paper-review-snapshot.tex), 1,752 lines, SHA-256 beginning `b750df1c104e`. I credit the corrections already present there, including the revised Corollary 1.4(b). I also inspected the 27-page PDF and compared the arguments with the six named project notes.

Current numbering differs from the question: the large-sieve result is **Lemma 4.11**, and the coverage exceptional-set result is **Theorem 5.4**.

“CORRECT” means that the stated argument survives this audit under its stated model; “GAP” identifies missing hypotheses, specification, or proof.

